  "instance_name": "artistic_ineptitude_stereotype",
  "label": "Artistic Ineptitude Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme implicitly references the stereotype that people who are 'unconventional' or 'unattractive' are somehow 'artistic' or 'creative' — a humorous inversion of the idea that artistic talent is linked to aesthetic appeal. This stereotype is rooted in the cultural perception that abstract or ugly art is 'artistic' and thus, by extension, the person who looks like it is 'artistic' — a form of ironic self-deprecation.",
